["FLC069","FLC127"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC069","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC127"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ae8e54e11e9105fc7e4866ee9a809176c3d3d8bf.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ae8e54e11e9105fc7e4866ee9a809176c3d3d8bf.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-10-18T20:58:00-04:00"}],"sent":"2026-10-19T09:56:00-04:00","effective":"2026-10-19T09:56:00-04:00","onset":"2026-10-19T09:56:00-04:00","expires":"2026-10-19T23:15:00-04:00","ends":null,"status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Melbourne FL","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 19 at 9:56AM EDT by NWS Melbourne FL","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nSt Johns River Near Astor affecting Lake and Volusia Counties.\n\n.Persistent northeast winds have caused river levels on the St Johns\nat Astor to rise into Moderate Flood Stage this morning. The river is\nforecast to climb slowly through Moderate Flood Stage through the end\nof this week.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Astor...Moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Moderate flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Astor.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 3.0 feet, Water approaches or may enter lowest homes\non or near Wildhog Road and nearby canals. Flooding reaches the\nparking lot of the Juno Trail Apartments. Flooding on portions of\nAlligator Road and Holiday Road. Lowest lying yards along Blue\nCreek are flooded. Roads at Astor Landing Campground and Lake\nDexter Boat Ramp begin to flood. Water enters lower homes closest\nto the river on McPherson Lane.\n\nAt 3.5 feet, Canals have overflowed into yards. Homes on or near\nWildhog and Bonnet roads become inaccessible with several inches of\nwater inside homes along the river and canals. Docks at Astor Bridge\nmarina and throughout Astor are completely submerged. Bartram Rd and\nHoliday Circle are inaccessible with yards completely submerged.\nClair Street is inaccessible. Roads flooded in South Moon Fish Camp,\ndocks and yards at condominiums on Juno Trail and water breaches the\nsea wall at Blair's Jungle Den.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 AM EDT Monday the stage was 3.0 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 2.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 8:30 AM EDT Monday was 3.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain steady above flood\nstage at 3.1 feet.\n- Flood stage is 2.3 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 1115 PM EDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 191356"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0003.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e267454960d05028ffb17d918dbfe239270f59aa.001.1,2026-10-18T09:11:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ec86a5b25822e52f8e371f554242bdd67483342f.001.1,2026-10-17T20:54:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7f1892302e6e287d1231cf4d12f60f419868b375.001.1,2026-10-17T09:04:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8aa4ca8f0a91b6616676b40340c36ef2b6f9788d.001.1,2026-10-16T21:21:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dfc8045564b49517706a7715d068ca72ead6ebb3.001.1,2026-10-16T10:44:00-04:0